(go/type RangeTable "RangeTable defines a set of Unicode code points by listing the ranges of\ncode points within the set. The ranges are listed in two slices\nto save space: a slice of 16-bit ranges and a slice of 32-bit ranges.\nThe two slices must be in sorted order and non-overlapping.\nAlso, R32 should contain only values >= 0x10000 (1<<16).\n" (struct
    ^{:line 22 :tag (slice Range16)} R16
    ^{:line 23 :tag (slice Range32)} R32
    ^{:line 24 :tag int} LatinOffset)) ; number of entries in R16 with Hi <= MaxLatin1




(go/type Range16 "Range16 represents of a range of 16-bit Unicode code points. The range runs from Lo to Hi\ninclusive and has the specified stride.\n" (struct
    ^{:line 30 :tag uint16} Lo
    ^{:line 31 :tag uint16} Hi
    ^{:line 32 :tag uint16} Stride))





(go/type Range32 "Range32 represents of a range of Unicode code points and is used when one or\nmore of the values will not fit in 16 bits. The range runs from Lo to Hi\ninclusive and has the specified stride. Lo and Hi must always be >= 1<<16.\n" (struct
    ^{:line 39 :tag uint32} Lo
    ^{:line 40 :tag uint32} Hi
    ^{:line 41 :tag uint32} Stride))














(go/type CaseRange "CaseRange represents a range of Unicode code points for simple (one\ncode point to one code point) case conversion.\nThe range runs from Lo to Hi inclusive, with a fixed stride of 1. Deltas\nare the number to add to the code point to reach the code point for a\ndifferent case for that character. They may be negative. If zero, it\nmeans the character is in the corresponding case. There is a special\ncase representing sequences of alternating corresponding Upper and Lower\npairs. It appears with a fixed Delta of\n\n\t{UpperLower, UpperLower, UpperLower}\n\nThe constant UpperLower has an otherwise impossible delta value.\n" (struct
    ^{:line 57 :tag uint32} Lo
    ^{:line 58 :tag uint32} Hi
    ^{:line 59 :tag d} Delta))




(go/type SpecialCase "SpecialCase represents language-specific case mappings such as Turkish.\nMethods of SpecialCase customize (by overriding) the standard mappings.\n" (slice CaseRange))

;; BUG(r): There is no mechanism for full case folding, that is, for
;; characters that involve multiple runes in the input or output.


